WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.498 --> 00:00:11.790
SUDHEERA VANGURI: Hi, everyone.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.700
Welcome to the
Document AI session.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.650
I'm Sudheera Vanguri, and I lead
the language and DocAI product

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.480
suite at Google Cloud.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.340
Today, I'm very
glad to be joined

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:27.720
by Nadia, a senior outbound
product manager at Workday.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.150
A quick runthrough
of the agenda today.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.090
I'll provide a brief
overview of Document AI

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.390
and how we convert documents
into business-ready structured

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.350
data.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.990
We'll then dive into
workplace approach

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:44.230
using DocAI to gain
operational efficiency.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.710
So let's dive right in.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.870
For centuries,
documents have been

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.240
foundational to our societies.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.060
We record histories,
establish laws,

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:57.810
legitimize trade, launch
companies, and confirm

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.190
identities with documents.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.069
The computer age has
introduced the idea

00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:06.890
of digital documents,
which now serve

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.740
as a backbone of our
modern societies.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:14.640
The power and value of
digital documents is immense.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.990
But for all the value that
these documents have created,

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:20.720
digital documents
still require work,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.160
not only in creating them, but
in processing these documents.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.710
Every company today
processes digital documents.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:33.940
The size and burden will
vary, as will the importance

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.470
of those documents.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:39.100
But no company is able to
escape the reality of what

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.130
we call digital manual labor.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.680
If you're watching this
session, you probably

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:49.870
know what I'm talking about, but
let me give you a few examples.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:53.740
Digital manual labor comprises
the work that many of us

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:57.910
do, but almost never shows
up in a job description.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:01.570
It is essential to the vast
majority of today's business

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:05.140
workflows, and it
captures the value of data

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.160
in those digital documents.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:14.430
It is also candidly a pain,
validating, checking, sorting,

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.930
keying, copy/pasting,
normalizing, et cetera.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.110
And with the continued
growth of digital workflows

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.410
and digital
transformation, we expect

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.760
this burden to only grow.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:32.900
For example, as the health
care industry has digitized,

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.160
the ratio of health care
administrators to physicians

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:43.490
has grown 35x, representing
the enormous and important work

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:47.090
of ensuring that our health
care records, prescriptions,

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:50.900
pre-authorizations, and
medical bills, all documents,

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.810
are processed properly.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:57.040
So let's talk about how we
want to help our customers

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:02.760
and their employees manage the
toil of digital manual labor.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.910
Document AI represents
Google's investment

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.580
to bring the power
of machine learning

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.770
to processing documents.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.540
You may have even seen
this slide before.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.280
In fact, we've shown this
slide to hundreds of customers,

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.760
and to be honest, sometimes
their reaction is not

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.940
very enthusiastic, and
that's because many of them

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:27.240
think that they've already
solved this problem

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.900
with other technologies.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.840
Awareness of the pain
for digital manual labor

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.220
is not new.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:36.800
For decades now,
smart people have

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.200
been working to
capture structured data

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.180
from digital documents.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:46.530
OCR, key value pair extraction,
template-based readers,

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.680
and other technologies
are now commonplace,

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.400
even so far that
the term OCR has

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:58.430
become a shorthand for document
extraction more generally.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.790
In short, if you try
digitizing documents,

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.810
you probably used one or
more of these or services

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:08.180
that are built on them.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.930
But if you've tried
using those technologies,

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.650
you've probably realized that
they aren't the full answer

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.110
for most business workflows.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:22.760
While they do what they say with
increasingly higher accuracy,

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:27.420
they also create new
kinds of digital work.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:30.960
Pre-processing, post-processing,
rules management,

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:34.980
and template management are
new kinds of toilsome tasks

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:40.960
that now often shift
burden to IT departments.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.020
The reason why these
legacy technologies

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:47.350
require supporting
labor, manual labor,

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.320
is because
understanding a document

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:54.340
is much more than
reading a document.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:57.400
In order to properly
understand a document,

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.960
humans do much more than
read words off the page.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.990
They bring knowledge
of what the document is

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:07.570
and what it should contain.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:13.210
They are able to interpret
different structures and words.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.430
They can connect
what they're reading

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:19.480
to other data in the
workflow or even from Google

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.510
to make sense of it, and so on.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:26.050
It's actually an
incredibly difficult task,

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:29.680
one that is harder to
automate than many expected.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.440
That's why, with
Document AI, we have

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.260
made it our goal
to turn documents

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:38.770
into business-ready
structured data.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.130
As we work closely with
our leading customers,

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.560
we realize that a
part of the problem

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:47.260
is that legacy
technologies are solving

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.900
a problem that is too simple.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:54.760
Yes, you can get some structured
data with a table parcel,

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:58.390
but we have heard that what
customers are looking for

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:01.580
is business-ready
structured data.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.240
In other words, they're
looking for a technology

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:09.670
that will read documents
in ways similar to humans.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.830
They are looking
for the confidence

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:15.610
that when they start
to automate processes,

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:19.030
they are not signing themselves
up to a different kind

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:22.740
of digital manual work.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:27.010
When we say business-ready,
what do we mean?

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:30.330
Of course, for each customer
and each business process,

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.390
the definition of
business-ready will vary,

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.850
but as we have moved
models into production

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.120
with more and more customers,
some consistent themes

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.590
have emerged.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:42.900
At a high level,
customers have asked

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.390
for an end-to-end
solution that is

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:49.050
business-ready for any
document and business-ready

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:51.680
for any document workflow.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.080
Business-readiness
for any document

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.050
means that DocAI can
process a given document

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:01.280
and deliver structured data
that a customer can immediately

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.200
trust and use.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.060
We have summarized this as four
C's, consistent and accurate

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:13.940
extraction, complemented with
other data, cross-border-ready,

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:16.620
and corrected as needed.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.380
I will spend the
next few minutes

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:21.970
covering what we mean
by each of these.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:24.220
But solving the
business problem doesn't

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:27.190
end with understanding
a single document.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:30.070
That is why we have
three more C's which

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:33.310
speak to the importance of
supporting the entire document

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.580
workflow; the ability
to custom build

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:42.370
new processes for a wide range
of new or long-tail documents,

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:46.360
the ability to comprehensively
orchestrate and execute tasks

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:49.630
across the document
workflow, and the ability

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:52.280
to constantly improve models.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:56.430
I will come back to these
at the very end of our time.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:59.540
I want to spend some time going
deeper into the first four

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.400
C's that we mentioned
about and how

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:06.580
we can get business-ready
data from a DocAI processor.

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:09.010
Again, these are those four C's.

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:11.890
Consistent and
accurate extraction,

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:15.970
complemented with other
data, cross-border-ready,

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:18.470
and corrected as needed.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:22.330
First, let's look at consistent
and accurate extraction.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:24.370
One of the wonderful
things about documents

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:27.050
is that they start
as blank slates.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:29.380
They can take on any
structure or design.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:32.380
Of course, this is also what
makes them hard to automate.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:35.230
But for any given
document type, you

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:39.010
may encounter a wide variety
of formats, versions, concepts,

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.890
words, et cetera, and
humans are naturally

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:44.210
able to make sense
of these differences,

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.715
but machines need
special training.

00:08:46.715 --> 00:08:48.340
And that's why we
are investing in what

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.610
we call specialized parsers,
machine learning models that

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:54.910
are built specifically for
any given document type.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:57.970
Here's a sample output from
the Document AI console,

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.390
and you'll see that the core
schema, supplier name, supplier

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:05.560
website, invoice ID don't
actually show up as text

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.390
on the document anywhere.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:10.720
Instead, these are concepts that
our models have been trained

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.610
over thousands and
thousands of samples

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:17.020
to recognize and then find
from one invoice to the next,

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:20.770
and this can be especially
powerful when there are, say,

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:23.620
multiple addresses which
belong to the supplier

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.540
versus the receiver.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.420
Specialized processors can
make these distinctions

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.160
that are ultimately
the difference

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:35.360
between business-ready data
and more digital manual labor.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:37.970
As you may know, we
have begun our journey

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:40.340
with specialized processors
focused on lending

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.110
and procurement workflows.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.820
In fact, we are
actively building

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.400
towards a library
of parsers for all

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:49.400
the world's most commonly
used business documents.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.880
And today, we are glad to
announce our latest edition

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.840
with Contract DocAI, specialized
document processors, what

00:09:56.840 --> 00:10:00.800
we call the most valuable
documents on the planet.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:05.000
For more details, please
check out the AI100 session.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.670
We are also proud to announce
that we are continuing

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:10.010
to expand the lending
DocAI portfolio

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:13.010
and now have about 50
specialized processes

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.390
available for use.

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:16.010
And there is much
more in flight,

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.650
which we'll be rapidly
releasing over the coming weeks

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:20.240
and months.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:24.920
OK, onto the next C,
complemented with other data.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:28.130
This is something we are
especially excited about.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:31.340
When the information is missing
or ambiguous on a document,

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:34.280
like a missing address
or entity name,

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:37.910
a human often needs to search
for it, often on Google.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:41.000
With DocAI, we are bringing
the power of Google Search

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.150
to help customers
understand their documents.

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:45.890
That means that the
same Google Knowledge

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:48.770
Graph that helps you find
the name or address or phone

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:51.350
number of a restaurant
you want to go to

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:54.870
can enrich your document
extraction with the right name,

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:57.120
address, or phone number.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.360
Here is a sample received from
a colleague's trip to Europe.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.730
If he were filling
out an expense report

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.800
and needed to input
merchant name,

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.950
he might struggle to choose
between some good options,

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:11.940
Angelina, Angelina
Paris, Angelina Rivoli.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.400
He might, say, take some
time to go to Google

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:19.290
and find the right entity
name, that is, Angelina Paris,

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:21.810
or he might guess and
move on, potentially

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:25.200
creating headaches for the
finance team down the line.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.660
With Document AI,
there is a better way.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.940
Our native integration
with Google Knowledge Graph

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.730
means that we can deliver
both the specific text

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:36.150
from the receipt as well as
Google's best understanding

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:38.310
of the actual name of
the restaurant that

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:40.930
operates at this address.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.250
Here's another example,
and in this use case,

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:46.330
the supplier address does not
appear anywhere on the receipt,

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.640
and this creates a choice
of either extra work

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.790
or potentially incomplete
or inconsistent data.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.190
However, Google
knows that the Office

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.710
Depot in Los Gatos
with this phone number

00:11:56.710 --> 00:12:00.970
is located at 15166
Los Gatos Boulevard,

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:04.690
so DocAI is able to enrich
this field, which would have

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.070
otherwise been returned empty.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:11.320
We are very proud to announce
that this Google Knowledge

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:13.930
Graph integration is aligned
with many of our core DocAI

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:16.620
processors, from
procurement to lending.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:20.340
The extraction of information
from invoices to receipts, bank

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.860
statements, pay
stubs, and more is now

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:25.620
enriched with the power of
Google's Knowledge Graph,

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:28.530
and we are actively working
to grow this capability out

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:31.740
for all relevant fields
across our entire portfolio

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:34.270
of parsers.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.250
The next C is
cross-border-readiness,

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:39.460
specifically the ability for
companies to process documents

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:42.500
in every language that
they do business in.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.732
Few of our customers do
business in only one country

00:12:44.732 --> 00:12:46.690
or language, and their
doc processing workflows

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:48.080
need to scale with them.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.350
And at Google, we have
taken a two-pronged approach

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:51.640
to this problem.

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:54.160
First, we are building
custom specialized processors

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.040
for some documents in
high-volume languages,

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.980
think Spanish invoices or
French identity documents,

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.780
and second, we are
building on Google's

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:04.450
longstanding leadership
in machine translation

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:07.000
by integrating translate
capabilities directly

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.110
into our specialized processors.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:11.320
This means that customers
will get instant access

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:15.940
to specialized doc processing
in hundreds of languages.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.705
Here's an example
of a French invoice.

00:13:17.705 --> 00:13:19.330
And again, you'll
see the full benefits

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:22.200
of schematized parsing, as
fields like supplier name,

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:24.700
supplier address are
extracted from the document,

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:28.570
even though the field names
themselves don't show up.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.280
As an aside, I want
to quickly highlight

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.920
amount of work that has gone
into the computer vision models

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.120
under DocAI.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:37.270
It's no small feat to be able to
read, say, the supplier address

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:39.650
off a document of this quality.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:41.620
In addition to our
specially trained models,

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.270
our integration with
Google Translate

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:45.520
means that customers can
now process documents

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.790
in over 100 languages, all of
those supported by the Google

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.503
Cloud translate service.

00:13:50.503 --> 00:13:52.420
Critically, while the
specially trained models

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.880
are of highest quality,
the translate-based models

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:58.640
have demonstrated
minimal quality losses.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:00.350
We're also pleased
to announce that many

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:01.730
of these cross-border
investments

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:03.830
are now available to our
customers, specifically

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.630
Procurement DocAI.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.340
The Procurement DocAI
team has specially

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:10.130
trained additional models
in six languages, primarily

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:11.780
European ones.

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:13.910
With Procurement
DocAI, we have also

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.620
integrated the
translate pipeline

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:17.420
into the invoice
and expense parsers,

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:20.480
expanding support to
100-plus languages.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:23.240
This feature is in preview
today and is also actively

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:28.030
being rolled out to all relevant
specialized parsers in future.

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:30.850
The fourth and final C for
today is corrected as needed.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:33.330
This highlights the reality
that for many workflows,

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:36.100
we will always need humans
involved to some degree.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.980
And while we can ease the
burden of digital manual labor,

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.130
we still need humans to
be the final reviewers

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:44.550
of critical and challenging
doc processing steps.

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:46.800
Our reviewer interface
brings the intuitiveness

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.870
and the simplicity of
Google interface design

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.720
into the hands of doc reviewers,
and we display the document

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:54.150
alongside the structure
data extraction,

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.910
highlight areas that
need more attention,

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:00.550
enable easy and on-document
corrections, and much more.

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:03.570
DocAI then returns for the
original and updated data

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:07.210
as part of the JSON output.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.520
As customers grow their
doc processing operations,

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:12.100
it is essential that they
are able to definitely manage

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:14.740
the wide range of settings
and priorities and tasks

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.750
and resources that
they oversee, and that

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:19.090
is why we have built the
manager interface as a control

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:22.450
panel for all of these needs,
and this is directly integrated

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:26.250
into the DocAI section
on the GCP console.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:29.190
We are now glad to announce
that the full range

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:32.010
of human-in-the-loop
functionality described below

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:34.950
is now fully available
for Lending DocAI,

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.560
expanding the coverage
that already existed with

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.420
Procurement DocAI.

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:42.610
We are aiming to make this fully
available for all of our doc

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.880
parsers, not only
for extraction,

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:48.570
but also for splitting
and classification.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:53.420
To recap, here are the summary
of all the new announcements

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:54.830
that we've made today.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:57.860
With Procurement DocAI, we
have Google Knowledge Graph

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.420
integration in GA.

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:02.870
We have custom-trained models
for high volume models in GA.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:05.840
We have translate
integration in preview.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:10.130
We have the Lending DocAI
with six new GA parsers

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:12.050
and 30 more in preview.

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:16.070
We have Contract DocAI
now available in preview.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.800
We have Google Knowledge
Graph integration available

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:22.370
on Lending DocAI, and we have
human-in-the-loop integration

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:25.610
also available in GA
for Lending DocAI.

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:28.790
We also have expanded language
support for Procurement DocAI.

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:34.480
For the last 10 minutes, we have
walked through many investments

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:37.420
we're making and improving
document processing workflows,

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:40.030
and we realize that for
our enterprise customers,

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:41.860
these workflows
are almost always

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:45.220
a part of a larger business
workflow; procure to pay,

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:49.420
expense to reimburse,
[INAUDIBLE] qualification,

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:52.030
insurance policy
underwriting, and so on.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.940
And that's why we are proud to
work with [INAUDIBLE] and SaaS

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:57.910
companies that are leaders
in helping customers execute

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.560
these business workflows.

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:02.440
One fantastic example of
this is our collaboration

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:04.900
with Workday, who
has been pioneering

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:09.069
the very use of Document AI
to reduce digital manual labor

00:17:09.069 --> 00:17:11.050
in daily business workflows.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:13.060
Today, I'm very
glad to be joined

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:17.290
by Nadia, a senior outbound
product manager at Workday.

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:20.140
Nadia has been a fantastic
collaborator and thought

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.660
partner for Document
Ai, and I'm very

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:25.630
excited for you to see
how she and her team

00:17:25.630 --> 00:17:29.260
have brought the best of DocAI
into the hands of their users.

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:31.030
I'm glad to introduce
Nadia to tell us

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:33.143
more about their journey.

00:17:33.143 --> 00:17:34.310
NADIA AQSA: Hello, everyone.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:35.380
My name is Nadia Aqsa.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.320
I'm the outbound product
manager for Workday Expenses,

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:41.400
and I'm so excited
to be here today.

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:43.740
In the five years that I've
been with Workday Expenses,

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:46.680
I don't think I've ever
met a customer that has not

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:50.100
asked how we are driving
operational efficiency

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.790
through machine learning.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:56.160
Whether it's OCR or
intelligent insights,

00:17:56.160 --> 00:18:00.810
automation is top of mind
for our 1,350-plus Expenses

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:02.880
customers.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.740
Today, I'll be
sharing a little bit

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:07.200
about what we've been
able to accomplish

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:10.350
with the help of DocAI
and more excitingly,

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:13.140
where we are headed next.

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.110
But before we go any
further, let me tell you

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.970
a little bit about Workday.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:20.450
Our mission is to deliver
value through our enterprise

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.780
management cloud that
brings financial management,

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:26.540
spend management, human
capital management,

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:31.220
and analytics together
in a single cloud.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:34.310
Our vision for the travel
and expense solution

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:36.830
is to put the
employee at the center

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:40.010
of a touchless
experience by eliminating

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:44.260
manual entry and cumbersome
review and approval processes.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:51.780
Earlier this year, Workday
combined Google Cloud's

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:56.070
Procurement DocAI solution with
our own document processing

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:59.820
machine learning models to
deliver an elevated experience

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:02.750
for our customers.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:06.700
These customers can now scan
receipts in five languages

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:09.340
and have the most
pertinent details

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.560
auto-populated for them.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:16.460
With 98% of Workday
Expenses customers

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:19.970
either creating or
editing expenses

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.250
on Workday mobile
in the past year,

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:26.990
this update made a lot
of people very happy.

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:31.665
Let's take a quick look at the
receipt scanning in action.

00:19:31.665 --> 00:19:33.290
We are in a demo
environment, and we're

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:36.110
going to use expense receipt
scanning service powered

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.500
by Google to scan a receipt
for our user, Dagmar,

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:41.930
who is an office
administrator in Germany.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:43.400
For the sake of
this demo, I have

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.130
switched her preferred
language to English.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:49.250
Dagmar went to a local
print job to copy documents,

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:52.370
and she saved the photo of the
receipt on her mobile device.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.800
She clicks the Scan
Receipt option, which

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.930
takes her to her photo album.

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:58.520
From there, she
selects the receipt

00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:01.250
that she wants to upload.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:04.370
The scan process has
kicked off, and it only

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:08.100
takes a few seconds to complete.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:11.600
Now that the scan is completed,
let's take a closer look.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.520
On the receipt, we see that
the merchant is not mentioned.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:17.240
We see the merchant address.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:18.630
We see the date.

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:22.540
We also see the amount
as well as a currency.

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:24.600
Now, let's scroll down further.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.820
The date, amount,
as well as currency

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.530
are populated as expected.

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:31.800
And to our surprise, the
Google Knowledge Graph

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:35.220
used the merchant's address
to derive the merchant name.

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:36.317
How cool is that?

00:20:36.317 --> 00:20:38.025
That's definitely
going to save her time.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.780
To complete the expense
report submission,

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:45.480
Dagmar will need to
select an expense item.

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:46.860
And I know what you're thinking.

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:49.648
Workday, when will you default
the expense item for her?

00:20:49.648 --> 00:20:51.940
Well, that's something that
we're working on right now,

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:54.470
and we hope to
release it very soon.

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:57.170
At this point, Dagmar can go
ahead and select the expense

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:59.840
and add it to her
expense report.

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:00.620
All right.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.440
Hopefully you were
also just as impressed

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:05.570
with the magic of
the Knowledge Graph.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:09.650
It's going to continue to be
instrumental towards delivering

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:13.320
a differentiated experience
for our customers.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:15.710
Now, some of you
may be wondering

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.820
why this is even a big deal.

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:21.890
I mean, you saw that we
scanned a few fields that

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:25.680
could probably be entered
manually pretty quickly.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.490
And if you're thinking
that way, that's OK.

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:30.900
I've had to explain this before.

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:36.560
So let me use a few numbers
to do the same thing.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:41.150
In 2019, so pre-COVID
era, our customers

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:47.520
uploaded 27 million expense
receipts into Workday.

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:52.740
If that manual receipt entry on
average takes about 3 minutes,

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:58.170
that is 1.35 million
hours of time

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:06.940
spent doing tedious tasks that
adds no real business value.

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:09.490
And post-COVID,
we actually expect

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:12.370
this number to be even higher.

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:17.320
Also, keep in mind that people
are not hired to do expenses,

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:21.340
and as an expenses PM, I
will be the first to admit

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:24.320
that no one even
enjoys doing expenses.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:26.840
So in other words,
in this day and age,

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:30.100
no one should have to enter
expense receipts manually

00:22:30.100 --> 00:22:33.190
because that time
is better spent

00:22:33.190 --> 00:22:36.090
on doing value added work.

00:22:36.090 --> 00:22:38.420
I hope this helps
you understand why

00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:41.900
we are so excited about
this, and with the help

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:43.460
of the Procurement
DocAI solution,

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:48.020
we expect to save customers
hundreds and thousands of hours

00:22:48.020 --> 00:22:52.330
and enable them to get back
to doing their real jobs.

00:22:52.330 --> 00:22:53.770
Now I'm going to
talk a little bit

00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:58.210
about what's coming up next
for us in relation to DocAI.

00:22:58.210 --> 00:23:00.070
By the end of this
year, our customers

00:23:00.070 --> 00:23:04.060
will be able to scan receipts
in 100-plus languages.

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:07.840
And although that, itself,
is a giant leap forward,

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:11.170
we are not stopping there.

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:13.350
We're looking at a
number of opportunities

00:23:13.350 --> 00:23:16.500
to create a touchless
expense entry experience,

00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:20.950
and I want to share a
couple of examples with you.

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:24.740
We will support fields
that are handwritten.

00:23:24.740 --> 00:23:28.000
So for example, you
have a meal receipt

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.160
that has a tip that's
been handwritten.

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:33.140
We'll be able to scan that and
auto-populate that for the user

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:36.280
so that they don't have to worry
about entering that manually.

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:39.260
In addition, we'll be
scanning additional fields,

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:42.220
such as a record
locator that's often

00:23:42.220 --> 00:23:44.230
found on a trip itinerary.

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:46.450
And what that will
help Workday do

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:49.240
is to use that as
a unique identifier

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:52.360
and link that to an existing
credit card transaction that's

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:55.990
already been imported into
Workday to accurately match

00:23:55.990 --> 00:24:00.630
the two so that the user does
not have to worry about that.

00:24:00.630 --> 00:24:03.570
These enhancements and
many more will further

00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:05.790
reduce the burden
of manual entry

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:10.320
and simplify expense
submission for our users.

00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:13.530
In addition, I want to mention
that aside from expense

00:24:13.530 --> 00:24:17.070
submitters, approvers
and reviewers are also

00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:20.190
two key additional
players in the expense

00:24:20.190 --> 00:24:22.990
to reimburse process.

00:24:22.990 --> 00:24:28.150
Today, many of our customers
painstakingly review expenses

00:24:28.150 --> 00:24:31.570
line by line, and they
do this to identify

00:24:31.570 --> 00:24:37.400
items that may be out of
policy or incorrectly coded.

00:24:37.400 --> 00:24:39.380
With the help of
Procurement DocAI,

00:24:39.380 --> 00:24:43.550
Workday will be able to provide
additional intelligent insights

00:24:43.550 --> 00:24:47.900
that will help the approver
and reviewer reduce

00:24:47.900 --> 00:24:50.420
the time that it takes to
get through that process.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:53.810
And that, in turn, will reduce
the time to reimbursement

00:24:53.810 --> 00:24:57.800
because everyone wants to
get their money ASAP, right?

00:24:57.800 --> 00:25:00.210
So how are we going to do this?

00:25:00.210 --> 00:25:02.180
Well, the Google
Knowledge Graph will

00:25:02.180 --> 00:25:05.480
help us identify the
category that a business

00:25:05.480 --> 00:25:07.440
establishment belongs to.

00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:10.040
And this information
will help determine

00:25:10.040 --> 00:25:12.410
if the expense is reimbursable.

00:25:12.410 --> 00:25:15.260
So for example, you
have an employee

00:25:15.260 --> 00:25:19.430
that goes to an adult
entertainment club and expenses

00:25:19.430 --> 00:25:21.650
that transaction as a meal.

00:25:21.650 --> 00:25:22.580
That does happen.

00:25:22.580 --> 00:25:24.320
Believe me.

00:25:24.320 --> 00:25:28.010
So we will take that
insight about the business

00:25:28.010 --> 00:25:32.240
establishment that's provided
by the Google Knowledge Graph,

00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:35.270
and we will flag that
expense for the reviewer

00:25:35.270 --> 00:25:38.900
so that they are able to
make an informed decision on

00:25:38.900 --> 00:25:43.790
whether or not that expense
should be reimbursed.

00:25:43.790 --> 00:25:46.520
Another common problem that
approvers and reviewers

00:25:46.520 --> 00:25:50.940
run into is ensuring that
the receipt is itemized

00:25:50.940 --> 00:25:52.940
so that it satisfies
the requirements

00:25:52.940 --> 00:25:55.370
of their back
office audit teams.

00:25:55.370 --> 00:25:57.920
With the help of
DocAI, we will plan

00:25:57.920 --> 00:26:01.190
to determine if the
receipt is in the format

00:26:01.190 --> 00:26:05.750
and has a content that satisfies
a criteria for valid documents.

00:26:08.900 --> 00:26:11.750
Now, Workday is also
looking at DocAI

00:26:11.750 --> 00:26:14.930
for supplier invoices
and contract scanning

00:26:14.930 --> 00:26:17.690
to improve document
understanding

00:26:17.690 --> 00:26:23.600
and enable users to make
better decisions more quickly.

00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:27.150
Our customers are incredibly
excited for what's to come,

00:26:27.150 --> 00:26:30.380
and I want to thank
Sudheera and the DocAI team

00:26:30.380 --> 00:26:33.390
for the invaluable work
that they've been doing.

00:26:33.390 --> 00:26:34.350
That's it for me.

00:26:34.350 --> 00:26:36.498
Now, over to Sudheera.

00:26:36.498 --> 00:26:38.290
SUDHEERA VANGURI: Thank
you so much, Nadia.

00:26:38.290 --> 00:26:41.260
We couldn't be more excited
about what you are building

00:26:41.260 --> 00:26:43.330
and how it will help
people with the work

00:26:43.330 --> 00:26:45.280
they're doing every single day.

00:26:45.280 --> 00:26:47.470
We spent most of our
time today looking

00:26:47.470 --> 00:26:50.110
at how DocAI can
take a given document

00:26:50.110 --> 00:26:53.140
and extract the
business-ready structured data

00:26:53.140 --> 00:26:56.500
and specifically how this
comes to life with receipts

00:26:56.500 --> 00:26:58.840
and expenses at Workday.

00:26:58.840 --> 00:27:02.380
Before we go, I want to spend
just a minute on last three

00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:03.130
C's.

00:27:03.130 --> 00:27:04.960
These are investments
we are making

00:27:04.960 --> 00:27:09.040
in DocAI that will ensure that
customers' document workflows

00:27:09.040 --> 00:27:11.690
are business-ready as well.

00:27:11.690 --> 00:27:14.390
Custom processors
reflect the reality

00:27:14.390 --> 00:27:17.600
that many customers
would need process--

00:27:17.600 --> 00:27:21.170
will need to process proprietary
or less common documents

00:27:21.170 --> 00:27:24.590
in addition to those for which
there are specialized parsers.

00:27:24.590 --> 00:27:27.020
And we want to make it
easy for those customers

00:27:27.020 --> 00:27:30.050
as well to quickly build
high-value, high-quality

00:27:30.050 --> 00:27:33.080
processors that work perfectly
well alongside the rest

00:27:33.080 --> 00:27:35.270
of the DocAI processors.

00:27:35.270 --> 00:27:37.190
Comprehensiveness
refers to the need

00:27:37.190 --> 00:27:40.160
to address more than just the
document extraction and review,

00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:43.730
and there are many challenges
upstream and downstream

00:27:43.730 --> 00:27:45.890
in the document
workflow, and we want

00:27:45.890 --> 00:27:48.750
to help customers
solve those too.

00:27:48.750 --> 00:27:50.150
And finally, we
want to make sure

00:27:50.150 --> 00:27:52.070
that DocAI is getting
more and more helpful

00:27:52.070 --> 00:27:53.570
